  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Render Is a Function Call",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A render is React calling your component function.",
            "It returns a description of UI. It is NOT a DOM update.",
            "UI = f(state); React computes the minimal DOM delta.",
            "Re-render ≠ DOM change: 50 renders, 0 mutations is normal."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Three Phases"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "Trigger: work scheduled",
              "Render: call + diff",
              "Commit: DOM mutations"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Render phase must be pure: no DOM writes, no fetches.",
            "No mutating props, state, or module variables.",
            "React may call it twice or throw the result away.",
            "Commit attaches refs and runs useLayoutEffect sync.",
            "useEffect runs after paint, not in commit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Elements vs Fibers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "const el = <Row id={1} />;  // jsx() call",
            "// { type: Row, props:{id:1}, key, ref }",
            "el.type === Row            // plain object"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Elements are immutable descriptions, made per render.",
            "The Fiber is the mutable work object kept across renders.",
            "Mount builds the whole tree; update diffs against the last."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "StrictMode (dev only)",
          "items": [
            "Components render twice on purpose.",
            "Surfaces impure render logic early.",
            "Never happens in production builds."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. What Starts a Render"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Trigger",
            "Source"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "own state",
              "useState / useReducer"
            ],
            [
              "parent rendered",
              "child renders by default"
            ],
            [
              "context changed",
              "Object.is on value"
            ],
            [
              "external store",
              "useSyncExternalStore"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Two words",
          "text": "Render = call the function. Commit = touch the DOM. Almost everything you tune lives in the first one."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Triggers, Batching, Diffing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. The Other Triggers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "forceUpdate, or a key change on the element.",
            "A key change is a remount, not a re-render.",
            "Props changing is NOT a trigger — the parent rendering is.",
            "Props are just what got passed down during that render."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Bail-out and Batching"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "setN(n)          // same value: may bail",
            "// React may still render once more first",
            "setA(1); setB(2) // one render, batched",
            "setC(c => c + 1) // needed inside a batch"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "React 18 batches timeouts, promises, native handlers too.",
            "Functional updater is required when next depends on prev.",
            "Setting state during your own render is legal.",
            "React re-runs the component at once, without committing."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Myth to kill",
          "text": "\"React re-renders only what changed.\" No — it re-renders the subtree by default, then diffs to minimise DOM work."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. The Diffing Goal"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Old tree + new tree → minimal set of DOM operations.",
            "General tree diff is O(n³); heuristics get React to O(n).",
            "Heuristic 1: different type means an entirely new tree.",
            "Heuristic 2: you hint stable identity with the key prop."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Match or Destroy"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Old → New",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "div → div",
              "keep node, patch props"
            ],
            [
              "div → span",
              "destroy + mount fresh"
            ],
            [
              "Profile → Feed",
              "state lost, refs detached"
            ],
            [
              "same slot, same type",
              "fiber and state kept"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "{cond ? <Input/> : <Input/>}   // state kept",
            "// same type, same slot = same fiber",
            "{cond ? <Input/> : <textarea/>} // reset"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "No keys = index diff",
          "items": [
            "Children are matched by position.",
            "Insert at the front: React sees every item change.",
            "Every row gets patched instead of one insert.",
            "Effects clean up on the destroyed subtree."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Fibers, Then Keys",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Where State Lives",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "State lives on the Fiber, keyed by (type, position).",
            "It survives exactly as long as type and slot hold.",
            "String/number children update in place via nodeValue.",
            "That text path is the cheapest case in the whole diff."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Fiber double buffering",
          "items": [
            "Two trees: current + workInProgress.",
            "Rendering is interruptible and resumable.",
            "Commit is a pointer flip, not a copy."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Bailout",
          "text": "If props are referentially equal and no state or context changed, React clones the child fibers and skips the subtree entirely."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Keys = Identity"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A key says which item in a list is which.",
            "Matching happens by identity, not by index.",
            "Stable: same item, same key, every render.",
            "Unique among siblings, and never random."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "11. Key Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Key",
            "Verdict"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "item.id",
              "correct"
            ],
            [
              "index",
              "static append-only lists only"
            ],
            [
              "Math.random()",
              "remount every render"
            ],
            [
              "uuid() inline",
              "state, focus, scroll lost"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "items.map(i => <Row key={i.id} {...i} />)",
            "// key is consumed by React",
            "// props.key inside Row is undefined",
            "<Row key={i.id} id={i.id} />  // pass twice"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Index-key bug",
          "items": [
            "A list of <input>s, reordered by index.",
            "Typed values stay glued to positions.",
            "Safe only with no reorder, filter, or item state."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Fragments take keys: <Fragment key={id}>.",
            "The <> shorthand cannot carry a key."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "12. Remount On Purpose"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<UserForm key={userId} />  // resets state",
            "// clearer than a syncing useEffect"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Same key and slot on two branches keeps state.",
            "Different keys force a clean reset.",
            "Keys are sibling-scoped, never global.",
            "Two separate lists may both use key='1'."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "React.memo: Stopping the Cascade",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "13. What memo Does",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "memo(Component) skips rendering on shallow-equal props.",
            "Object.is is applied per prop key — no deep compare.",
            "Nested objects are compared by reference only.",
            "It breaks the parent-renders-child-renders chain."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "14. Custom Comparator"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "memo(Row, (prev, next) =>",
            "  prev.id === next.id)  // true = SKIP",
            "// opposite of shouldComponentUpdate"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "memo cannot stop",
          "items": [
            "The component's own state updates.",
            "A context it consumes changing.",
            "A key change — that is a remount."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "15. One Unstable Prop"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<MemoRow onSelect={() => select(id)} />",
            "// new fn each render: memo never hits",
            "<MemoRow style={{}} data={[...rows]} />"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Inline arrow, object, and array = fresh reference.",
            "Memoization is all-or-nothing at the boundary."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "16. children Escape Hatch"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<Wrapper><Expensive /></Wrapper>",
            "// children built by the OUTER parent",
            "// Wrapper re-renders, Expensive does not"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The children reference stays stable for free.",
            "No memo, no deps array, no comparison cost."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "17. Is It Worth It?"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Case",
            "memo?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "genuinely expensive",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "renders often, same props",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "large subtree root",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "leaf rendering one <span>",
              "no, costs more"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "React Compiler",
          "text": "React 19+ auto-inserts memoization, so most hand-written memo/useMemo/useCallback is unnecessary in compiled code."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "useMemo: Caching Values",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "18. Signature",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const v = useMemo(() => calc(a,b), [a,b])",
            "// caches the RESULT between renders",
            "// deps compared with Object.is, one by one"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Any dep change re-runs the factory during render.",
            "Empty deps = compute once for the instance lifetime.",
            "No deps array = no memoization at all, plus a lint error."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "19. Two Distinct Jobs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Job",
            "Payoff"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "skip slow compute",
              "CPU time saved"
            ],
            [
              "keep object identity",
              "downstream memo hits"
            ],
            [
              "feed a dep array",
              "effect stops re-firing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const s = useMemo(() => ({width}), [width])",
            "// stable ref for a memo'd child"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "20. Not a Guarantee"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A cache with one entry and no promises.",
            "React may discard it, e.g. to free offscreen memory.",
            "So the factory must be pure and safe to redo.",
            "Code must still work if every useMemo recomputed."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Hard rules",
          "items": [
            "Never put side effects inside — it runs during render.",
            "Never use it for correctness, only for cost.",
            "The cache is per component instance.",
            "Remount or key change throws it away."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "21. Measure First"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "console.time('calc'); calc(a,b);",
            "console.timeEnd('calc');  // calc: 0.04ms",
            "// then throttle CPU 4-6x in DevTools"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Under ~1ms and not feeding a memo boundary? Skip the hook — it costs more than the work it saves."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "useCallback: Caching Functions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "22. It Is Just useMemo",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "useCallback(fn, deps)",
            "// is exactly the same as",
            "useMemo(() => fn, deps)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The purpose is referential stability, not speed.",
            "Creating a closure is cheap.",
            "The real cost is the re-render it triggers downstream."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "23. When It Earns Its Keep"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Consumer",
            "Wrap?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "prop to a memo'd child",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "useEffect / useMemo dep",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "argument to a custom hook",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "<button onClick={cb}>",
              "no gain at all"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "24. Stale Closure Hazard"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "useCallback(() => setC(count+1), [])",
            "// captures count = 0 forever",
            "useCallback(() => setC(c => c+1), [])",
            "// updater keeps deps empty honestly"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Deps must include every reactive value the fn reads.",
            "The exhaustive-deps lint rule is your only guard."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Chain rule",
          "text": "A useCallback is stable only if all of its own deps are stable. One unstable dep poisons the whole chain up the tree."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "25. Better Than Wrapping"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "For effects, move the function INSIDE the effect.",
            "A ref-based 'latest callback' gives a permanent handle.",
            "useEffectEvent reads fresh values and is never a dep.",
            "Custom hooks: wrap what you return — callers cannot."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Anti-pattern",
          "items": [
            "Blanket-wrapping every handler 'just in case'.",
            "Adds deps arrays, allocations, lint noise.",
            "Zero gain if nothing downstream is memo'd."
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Context & State Colocation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "26. Context Ignores memo",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every consumer re-renders when value changes by Object.is.",
            "memo does NOT block a context update.",
            "A memo'd component sitting in between changes nothing.",
            "Deeply nested consumers still re-render."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "27. Classic Provider Bug"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<Ctx.Provider value={{user, setUser}}>",
            "// new object every provider render",
            "const v = useMemo(() => ({user, setUser}),",
            "                  [user])   // the fix"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "28. Split By Frequency"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<StateCtx.Provider value={state}>",
            "  <DispatchCtx.Provider value={dispatch}>",
            "// useReducer dispatch never changes"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Action-only consumers then never re-render.",
            "Context has no selector — it is all or nothing.",
            "You cannot subscribe to one field of the value."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need selection?",
            "Use"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "one field only",
              "useSyncExternalStore"
            ],
            [
              "big shared state",
              "Zustand / Redux"
            ],
            [
              "stay in context",
              "use-context-selector"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Fit",
          "items": [
            "Good: theme, locale, auth — low frequency.",
            "Bad: mouse position, form input.",
            "A provider re-render hits kids by the normal rule.",
            "Pass children through to dodge that."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "29. Move State Down"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The cheapest re-render fix is a smaller render scope.",
            "Before: input state at page root, whole tree per keystroke.",
            "After: extract <SearchInput> owning its own state.",
            "Splitting beats memo — zero runtime, no deps arrays."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "function Page() {",
            "  return <><SearchInput/><Big/></>",
            "}",
            "// Big never re-renders while typing"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lift expensive subtrees UP: pass as children or props.",
            "Created by an outer component, so never re-created."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Structure First, Then Measure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "30. Derive, Don't Duplicate",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const full = first + ' ' + last;  // derive",
            "// not useState + useEffect sync",
            "// that costs an extra render pass"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never useEffect + setState to mirror props.",
            "Use the key-reset trick or compute during render.",
            "useReducer: one dispatch, one render, many fields.",
            "React 18 batches anyway — clarity is the real win."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "31. Structural Escapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Problem",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "per-keystroke renders",
              "uncontrolled input + ref"
            ],
            [
              "10,000 rows",
              "virtualize, render 20"
            ],
            [
              "heavy list while typing",
              "useDeferredValue"
            ],
            [
              "slow non-urgent update",
              "startTransition"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "react-window / TanStack Virtual beat memoizing rows.",
            "Refs give values on submit with zero renders."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "32. DevTools Profiler"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Record an interaction, read the flamegraph: width = time.",
            "Enable 'Record why each component rendered'.",
            "Reasons: props / state / hooks / parent / context.",
            "'Highlight updates' shows the cascade live on screen."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "33. Programmatic Timing"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<Profiler id='list' onRender={log}>",
            "// (id, phase, actualDuration,",
            "//  baseDuration, startTime, commitTime)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "baseDuration = the cost with no memoization at all.",
            "The gap to actualDuration is what memo buys you.",
            "Always profile a production build — dev is much slower.",
            "Throttle CPU 4x or 6x to model a real device."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "34. Three Different Costs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "too many renders",
              "memo / colocate"
            ],
            [
              "one slow render",
              "useMemo / split"
            ],
            [
              "slow commit",
              "fewer DOM mutations"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Scale, not vibes",
          "text": "60 renders at 0.1ms is fine; 2 renders at 200ms is the bug. Memoize the measured bottleneck — every memo is code you keep correct forever."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs & First Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "35. The Tool Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Memoizes",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "memo",
              "a component",
              "prop compare + tree"
            ],
            [
              "useMemo",
              "a value",
              "closure + deps + memory"
            ],
